  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "runtime-dirs-not-shipped",
      "lines": [
        "resources/ is read at run time and is not in the shipped file set: lib/Editor/Fb2Genres.php:23 reaches it through dirname(__DIR__, 2), as 3 further places do.",
        "  A release ships only the paths of the keep set (the ncmake core and ncmake.mk), so the tarball lacks it and the app fails in the code that reads it, while the build and the packing pass. In ncmake.mk, keep_extra += resources ships it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "app-id",
      "lines": [
        "The app id is ebookreader, the checkout directory is nextcloud_ebook_reader.",
        "  The server finds an app by its directory name, so the installed directory has to be named after the id. A checkout can be named anything, which is why this is a note and not a defect - but a tarball built from this directory name would not load."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node 22 stated in ci.yml, release.yml, within package.json engines.node ^20.11.0 || ^22 || ^24.",
        "  Not stated in .nvmrc, so nothing keeps the other places from drifting away from it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (eslint.config.js), Psalm (psalm.xml), PHPUnit (phpunit.xml), PHP-CS-Fixer (.php-cs-fixer.dist.php).",
        " No Stylelint configuration: stylesheets are unchecked, and a mistake in CSS fails silently instead of loudly.",
        " No REUSE configuration: licensing is not machine-checkable, which the App Store and every distribution ask for.",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence AGPL-3.0-or-later (appinfo/info.xml, package.json, composer.json).",
